"""/*
 * `:focus`, not `:focus-visible`. The component moves focus here deliberately
 * after a check-in, and Chrome does not treat a programmatic focus as
 * focus-visible when the last interaction was a pointer -- so a mouse or touch
 * user's focus relocated from the button to this paragraph with nothing on
 * screen saying so, and their next Tab started somewhere unexpected.
 *
 * Safe here because the element is only reachable via `tabIndex={-1}`: the only
 * ring this adds beyond the keyboard case is on a direct click of the message
 * itself, which is the one place a ring is honest anyway.
 */
.checkin-feedback:focus {
  outline: 3px solid #f5d0fe;
  outline-offset: 2px;
}""")
